ns using short sequence motifs.</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><year>2003</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>3635</fpage><lpage>3641</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12824383</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B5"><label>5</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hjerrild</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Stensballe</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Rasmussen</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name><name><surname>Kofoed</surname><given-names>CB</given-names></name><name><surname>Blom</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Sicheritz-Pont&#x000e9;n</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Larsen</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Jensen</surname><given-names>ON</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Identification of phosphorylation sites in protein kinase A substrates using artificial neural networks and mass spectrometry.</article-title><source>J. Proteome Res</source><year>2004</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>426</fpage><lpage>433</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15253423</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B6"><label>6</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blom</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Sicheritz-Pont&#x000e9;n</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Gupta</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Gammeltoft</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Brunak</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prediction of post-translational glycosylation and phosphorylation of proteins from the amino acid sequence</article-title><source>Proteomics</source><year>2004</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>1633</fpage><lpage>1649</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15174133</pub-id